## Ornithe Standard Libraries 0.23.0

OSL 0.23.0 supports Minecraft versions between Alpha 1.0.1_01 and Release 1.14.4.

## Core 0.12.0

### Namespaced Identifiers

New functionality has been added to namespaced identifiers, and a change has been made to equality checks.

```java
NamespacedIdentifier {

	// Returns the char used as the separator in the String-representation of the namespaced identifier.
	// This separator is also used to check equality of namespaced identifiers.
	char separator();

	// Returns a copy of this namespaced identifier with the given namespace.
	NamespacedIdentifier namespaced(String namespace);

	// Returns a copy of this namespaced identifier where the identifier is a substring of this identifier.
	NamespacedIdentifier subidentifier(int beginIndex);

	// Returns a copy of this namespaced identifier where the identifier is a substring of this identifier.
	NamespacedIdentifier subidentifier(int beginIndex, int endIndex);

}
```

New functionality has also been added to the `NamespacedIdentifiers` utility class, in the form of various `isValid` methods that return a `boolean` result. These complement the various `validate` methods that throw an exception on invalid input.

```java
NamespacedIdentifiers {

	// Returns whether the given namespaced identifier conforms to spec (only chars a-z0-9-._/ allowed).
	static boolean isValid(NamespacedIdentifier identifier);

	// Returns whether the given String is a valid namespace.
	static boolean isValidNamespace(String namespace);

	// Returns whether the given String is a valid identifier.
	static boolean isValidIdentifier(String identifier);

	// Returns whether the given char is allowed in the String representation of a namespaced identifier.
	static boolean isCharAllowed(char chr);

}
```

A change has been made to the `NamespacedIdentifiers#equals(NamespacedIdentifier, NamespacedIdentifier)` method. It now also checks equality of the `NamespacedIdentifier#separator()` result in addition to equality of the `NamespacedIdentifier#namespace()` and `NamespacedIdentifier#identifier` results.

### Topological Sorting

Added `TopoSort` utility class, which can perform as topological sort on a list of nodes, given all the incoming edges for each node.

## Executors 0.1.1

Added `ReentrantDirectExecutor`, an `Executor` that handles reentrance with a queue. This is internal API for the Resource Loader API.

## Block States 0.2.0

### Block Entity Extension

- Fixed several server-side Mixin issues that caused crashes in dedicated server environments in 12w42a and below.
- To aid in fixing above issue, some methods were added to `BlockEntity` on the server side in 12w42a and below.

```java
BlockEntity {

	// Returns the block at this block entity's position in the world.
	Block getBlock();

	// Returns the metadata of the block at this block entity's position in the world.
	int getBlockMetadata();

}
```

## Entities 0.1.2

Fixed a `NoSuchMethodError` in 1.9-1.10 when registering a spawn egg through `EntityTypeRegistry#registerSpawnEgg(EntityType, int, int)`.

## Networking 0.11.0 & 0.12.0

### Channel Identifiers

Serialization of channel identifiers has been changed to be more consistent and versatile.

Previously, the way channels identifiers were converted to and from `String`s was different in 1.13-pre2 and below vs 1.13-pre4 and above.

In 1.13-pre4 and above, Vanilla uses `Identifier`s for custom payload channels, and OSL does as well. As such, there is no special handling for `String` conversions, and the standard colon-separated format is used: `<namespace>:<identifier>`.

```java
ChannelIdentifiers.from("example", "cookie"); // String representation -> "example:cookie"
```


